<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Mayo Clinic Cloud Solution - Google Cloud</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      background-color: #f8f9fa;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 20px;
    }
    header {
      background-color: #4285f4;
      color: white;
      padding: 20px;
      text-align: center;
    }
    section {
      background: white;
      padding: 20px;
      margin: 20px auto;
      max-width: 800px;
      box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
    }
    h2 {
      color: #333;
    }
    ul {
      padding-left: 20px;
    }
    footer {
      text-align: center;
      margin-top: 40px;
      color: #888;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <header>
    <h1>Mayo Clinic Cloud Solution</h1>
    <h3>Powered by Google Cloud</h3>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2>Organization</h2>
    <p><strong>Mayo Clinic</strong> — A leading nonprofit American academic medical center focused on integrated clinical practice, education, and research.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Cloud Provider</h2>
    <p><strong>Google Cloud Platform (GCP)</strong> — Chosen for its scalability, HIPAA compliance, AI/ML capabilities, and healthcare-specific tools like the Cloud Healthcare API.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Use Case</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Processing large-scale Electronic Health Records (EHRs)</li>
      <li>Managing and analyzing medical imaging and genomics data</li>
      <li>Running AI analytics for clinical and academic research</li>
      <li>Enabling secure telemedicine and video consultation services</li>
      <li>Providing collaborative platforms for clinicians and researchers</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Implementation Example</h2>
    <p><strong>Hybrid Cloud Architecture:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Private Cloud / On-Premise:</strong> Sensitive patient data (PHI) is stored and processed securely on-premise or in a private cloud infrastructure.</li>
      <li><strong>Public Cloud (Google Cloud):</strong> Research workloads, non-sensitive analytics, and AI/ML models are processed in GCP.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>This setup ensures security and scalability while complying with regulatory standards.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Risk Mitigation</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Encryption:</strong> Data encrypted in transit and at rest using Google-managed or customer-managed encryption keys (CMEK).</li>
      <li><strong>IAM Policies:</strong> Role-based access control to ensure least privilege access.</li>
      <li><strong>Compliance:</strong> Full adherence to HIPAA, GDPR, and other healthcare regulations.</li>
      <li><strong>Monitoring:</strong> Real-time threat detection and compliance auditing with Google Cloud Security Command Center.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <p>© 2025 Mayo Clinic – Cloud Architecture Summary</p>
  </footer>

</body>
</html>
